    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d674">

                <pb facs="0819" n="533" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg533"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 300.115/11026</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Foreign Trade Adviser of the Department of
                        State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Letcher</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to Mr.</hi>
                    
                        <hi rendition="#italic">A. W. Faber</hi>
                    
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-12-19">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 19, 1916</hi>
                        </date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The receipt is acknowledged of your letter
                    of December 15, 1916, in which you make inquiry concerning the results obtained
                    by Mr. Wyvell while in England endeavoring to obtain
                    permits from the British authorities to ship goods of German origin.<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d674-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>In reply I beg to advise you that only one case presented by Mr.
                        Wyvell, namely, the case of the Harrison Glove Company,
                    was granted. All other cases were either rejected or consideration thereof
                    refused.</p>
                <p>I regret, therefore, that I can do nothing further to assist you in the
                    premises.</p>
                <p>Very truly yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marion Letcher</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
